In .NET 10, MAUI adopts **edge-to-edge** rendering on Android by default, which makes the old `WindowSoftInputModeAdjust.Resize` ineffective. Here's how to fix it:

## Recommended: Use Keyboard Insets (Edge-to-Edge compatible)

In your `Platforms/Android/MainActivity.cs`, listen to insets and adjust your layout padding:

```csharp
using Android.Views;
using AndroidX.Core.View;

// In OnCreate, after base call:
ViewCompat.SetOnApplyWindowInsetsListener(Window.DecorView, new InsetsListener(this));

class InsetsListener : Java.Lang.Object, IOnApplyWindowInsetsListener
{
    readonly Activity _activity;
    public InsetsListener(Activity activity) => _activity = activity;

    public WindowInsetsCompat OnApplyWindowInsets(View v, WindowInsetsCompat insets)
    {
        var imeInsets = insets.GetInsets(WindowInsetsCompat.Type.Ime());
        var navInsets = insets.GetInsets(WindowInsetsCompat.Type.NavigationBars());
        var bottom = Math.Max(imeInsets.Bottom, navInsets.Bottom);

        // Adjust the content view padding
        var content = _activity.FindViewById(Android.Resource.Id.Content);
        content.SetPadding(0, 0, 0, bottom);

        return insets;
    }
}
```

## Simpler Alternative: Opt out of edge-to-edge

If you don't need edge-to-edge, disable it and use the classic approach in `MainActivity.cs`:

```csharp
[Activity(..., WindowSoftInputMode = SoftInput.AdjustResize)]
public class MainActivity : MauiAppCompatActivity
{
    protected override void OnCreate(Bundle? savedInstanceState)
    {
        base.OnCreate(savedInstanceState);
        // Disable edge-to-edge so AdjustResize works again
        AndroidX.Activity.EdgeToEdge.Disable(Platform.CurrentActivity);
    }
}
```

## Quick Check: KeyboardAutoManagerScroll

MAUI's built-in auto-scroll (enabled by default) works if your `Entry`/`Editor` is inside a `ScrollView`. For a chat layout:

```xml
<Grid RowDefinitions="*,Auto">
    <ScrollView Grid.Row="0">
        <CollectionView ItemsSource="{Binding Messages}" ... />
    </ScrollView>
    <HorizontalStackLayout Grid.Row="1">
        <Entry Placeholder="Type a message..." />
        <Button Text="Send" />
    </HorizontalStackLayout>
</Grid>
```

---

**TL;DR:** The insets approach is the proper .NET 10 fix. If you just want things working quickly, disable edge-to-edge with the second approach.
